  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_65e9f005a2d54f34855973ef7482f538",
      "statement": "The saved-selection document is a single `TransitSelections` value of shape `{commutes: {toWork: TransitPointSelections, toHome: TransitPointSelections}}`, where each `TransitPointSelections` carries exactly four canonical fields — `busStops`, `subwayStations`, `selectedBusStopIds`, `selectedSubwayStationId` — produced by the Zod transform, and `COMMUTE_CONTEXTS = [\"toWork\", \"toHome\"]` is a closed Zod enum so indexing `commutes[commute]` is exhaustive by construction.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/contracts/src/transitSettings.ts#L27-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:24dc57e2ad3aff1e14b509dee4f079cc742fb3d807ff740d7dc870dfc20f82b6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/contracts/src/transitSettings.ts#L8-L10",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2fd2fe12b6aab02698570df4866fa2b19aff80a319ee6aee168afae9820b4bd2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ced06b3598df4938b80c416c48aa5ada",
      "statement": "The two selection kinds are deliberately asymmetric: bus stops are multi-watch (an unbounded saved `busStops` list plus a `selectedBusStopIds` subset capped by `MAX_SELECTED_BUS_STOPS = 4`, each selected stop rendering its own arrival section), while subway stations are single-watch (unbounded saved list, single nullable `selectedSubwayStationId`). This asymmetry is product scope from DESIGN.md §1 and is why only the bus path required a v2 multi-watch migration.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://DESIGN.md#L12-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:17d200a74ad4dd90540783f0d7872b1bace863dddc3dbac083be2dc676dc454e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/contracts/src/transitSettings.ts#L5-L6",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:feaeab93b18992b621eef6d1e3868c6e143e6e01bd07405476b4b3712c20c059:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_65725268fd0246c9852116f6fb449adb",
      "statement": "`transitSelectionsSchema` is a `z.union` of the per-commute document (`{commutes: {toWork, toHome}}`) and a legacy flat point-selection document; the outer transform promotes a flat document by placing the same point-selection object into both `toWork` and `toHome`. This one-time duplication is the only operation that ever writes both contexts at once and implements DESIGN.md's rule that legacy single-storage stops and stations are preserved in both commute contexts.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://DESIGN.md#L24-L25",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:447c241bb8a1acfa2d024502e8e90119a7ecc42f9c0ebd93b3f621f1aa5a8518:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/contracts/src/transitSettings.ts#L47-L65",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:57bfcf095c3af17a72b5bbf40deb9b70762907ac6c01f9367ad440916ef6609a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_79f14c5168854c03bcb1a110bbb4ca7a",
      "statement": "The v2 multi-watch migration runs inside `transitPointSelectionsSchema`: the input schema declares both `selectedBusStopIds` (array, capped) and the legacy singular `selectedBusStopId` (nullable) as optional, and the transform produces the canonical `selectedBusStopIds` list by taking the array when present, otherwise wrapping a non-null singular id into a one-element list, otherwise an empty list, deduplicating through a `Set` in every case; `selectedSubwayStationId` is normalized with `?? null`. Because the point schema is the union member, the oldest shape — a flat document carrying only `selectedBusStopId` — migrates through both rungs in a single `safeParse` call.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/contracts/src/transitSettings.test.ts#L47-L67",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6a1786fa587bef4c3c9d69712601e79bf1b902ba23a3d0cf0857a6223c927968:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/contracts/src/transitSettings.ts#L12-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d4182bf4925b65d88ad379b35c278cd78d05860675f405f755fdc8961331fd51:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_217ee6b92c9c47839d5e1dead48e3e6e",
      "statement": "`MAX_SELECTED_BUS_STOPS = 4` is applied with two different semantics: the schema's `.max(MAX_SELECTED_BUS_STOPS)` makes a document with five or more watched ids fail to parse (asserted by `safeParse(...).success === false` in the contract test), while the storage layer's normalizer truncates with `.slice(0, MAX_SELECTED_BUS_STOPS)`. Consequence: changing the constant alters what the shared schema rejects from the server, so lowering it is a data-compat break for previously-valid stored documents re-parsed in `packages/db` and the browser client.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/web/src/hooks/transitSelectionStorage.ts#L55-L57",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5e14fa95ac998d4cd46ced312739d1d3341ea7df8484a38a84917b404a547d52:"
        },
