    {
      "id": "claim_18563c412f8c421aaaf28be90a553291",
      "statement": "Per AGENTS.md's boundary rule that localStorage values are untrusted and parsed with Zod, `loadTransitSelections` resolves an injectable store (`Pick<Storage, \"getItem\" | \"setItem\">`, defaulting to `window.localStorage`, and returning the empty document when `typeof window === \"undefined\"` for SSR safety), reads the key, JSON-parses, and validates with `transitSelectionsSchema.safeParse` so the migration transforms apply. `parseJson` swallows only `SyntaxError` (returning `null`) and rethrows anything else; every failure path — no window, missing key, bad JSON, failed Zod parse — returns `EMPTY_SELECTIONS` and the function never throws, which is what lets `useTransitSelections` seed state with it as a lazy `useState` initializer on the first render.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://AGENTS.md#L26-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:20d33837dddc024079c9cf88e7c42fa9a24d5eff382438bacb2ca012f8120f5e:"
        },
        {
