    {
      "id": "claim_db9bf9e2fad74896850a491990c9c4e1",
      "statement": "The authenticated lane reuses the same schema rather than a parallel definition: the browser parses `GET /api/settings` with `transitSettingsSnapshotSchema` (`{version: non-negative integer, selections: TransitSelections | null}`), the API validates `PUT` bodies with `transitSettingsUpdateSchema` (which requires a non-null `selections`), and `packages/db`'s `toStored` re-parses the `user_settings.selections` jsonb column with `transitSelectionsSchema`, throwing `InvalidStoredSettingsError` on a bad row instead of repairing it. `SettingsController` maps a failed body parse to `INVALID_SETTINGS` (400) and `SettingsVersionConflictError` to `SETTINGS_VERSION_CONFLICT` (409); a fresh account reads as `{version: 0, selections: null}`, the signal the client uses to bootstrap from the anonymous document.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/api/src/settings/settings.controller.ts#L82-L112",
