    {
      "id": "claim_dafb93010fdc4c3a872b12a88469ebb9",
      "statement": "The document model is pinned at four layers: `packages/contracts/src/transitSettings.test.ts` asserts the migration ladder (flat document lands in both commutes, singular `selectedBusStopId` yields a one-element list in both contexts), dedupe during migration, over-cap rejection, and malformed-array rejection; `apps/web/src/App.test.tsx` asserts end-to-end commute independence for both modes and that a seeded legacy `selectedBusStopId` document produces an active selection in both tabs on the next render; `apps/web/src/hooks/useTransitSelections.test.tsx` asserts hook-level independence (adding stops to `toHome` leaves `toWork` untouched) and cap behavior up to four watched ids; and `packages/db/src/repository.integration.test.ts` asserts the jsonb round trip and compare-and-swap version enforcement behind the authenticated lane.",
